 "sentences": [
  {
   "text": "Four soldiers pick up a thirty-ton tank...",
   "words": [
    0,
    6
   ],
   "subject": "lou"
  },
  {
   "text": "and set it down in a field like a suitcase!",
   "words": [
    7,
    16
   ],
   "subject": "lou"
  },
  {
   "text": "Two Frenchmen on bicycles stop dead.",
   "words": [
    17,
    22
   ],
   "subject": "farmer"
  },
  {
   "text": "A soldier winks: \"Americans are very strong.\" You see, that tank is made of rubber.",
   "words": [
    23,
    37
   ],
   "subject": "lou"
  },
  {
   "text": "And these soldiers are painters, set designers and art students!",
   "words": [
    38,
    47
   ],
   "subject": "lou"
  },
  {
   "text": "Their job: make the enemy believe a whole army is here...",
   "words": [
    48,
    58
   ],
   "subject": "lou"
  },
  {
   "text": "when there's nobody.",
   "words": [
    59,
    61
   ],
   "subject": "lou"
  },
  {
   "text": "One rule: nobody gets closer than a quarter mile.",
   "words": [
    62,
    70
   ],
   "subject": "lou"
  },
  {
   "text": "Up close, it's all fake.",
   "words": [
    71,
    75
   ],
   "subject": "lou"
  },
  {
   "text": "From far away, it's an army!",
   "words": [
    76,
    81
   ],
   "subject": "lou"
  },
  {
   "text": "By day they blow up tanks, trucks and cannons, and a bulldozer even draws the track marks!",
   "words": [
    82,
    98
   ],
   "subject": "lou"
  },
  {
   "text": "At night, one truck rolls by...",
   "words": [
    99,
    104
   ],
   "subject": "sound_op"
  },
  {
   "text": "and you hear a hundred tanks!",
   "words": [
    105,
    110
   ],
   "subject": "sound_op"
  },
  {
   "text": "Engines, tracks, shouted orders, all from a speaker you can hear fifteen miles away!",
   "words": [
    111,
    124
   ],
   "subject": "sound_op"
  },
  {
   "text": "On the radio, they even copy the way real operators tap their Morse code, like forging a signature.",
   "words": [
    125,
    142
   ],
   "subject": "radio_op"
  },
  {
   "text": "And in the village café, they sew on fake patches and let slip fake secrets...",
   "words": [
    143,
    157
   ],
   "subject": "lou"
  },
  {
   "text": "for the spies.",
   "words": [
    158,
    160
   ],
   "subject": "lou"
  },
  {
   "text": "A real sergeant laughs: \"So now we fight wars with carnival balloons?\" Then comes the big river.",
   "words": [
    161,
    177
   ],
   "subject": "sergeant"
  },
  {
   "text": "In six days, the real army has to cross it.",
   "words": [
    178,
    187
   ],
   "subject": "lou"
  },
  {
   "text": "So the ghost army blows up six hundred tanks, ten miles to the south.",
   "words": [
    188,
    201
   ],
   "subject": "sound_op"
  },
  {
   "text": "The enemy photographs them, listens to them, spies on them...",
   "words": [
    202,
    211
   ],
   "subject": "interpreter"
  },
  {
   "text": "and sends every gun at the balloons!",
   "words": [
    212,
    218
   ],
   "subject": "lou"
  },
  {
   "text": "Meanwhile, up north, the real army crosses the river with barely a shot fired.",
   "words": [
    219,
    232
   ],
   "subject": "sergeant"
  },
  {
   "text": "You see, it's the pillow-under-the-blanket trick: while everyone watches the bed, the kid is already outside.",
   "words": [
    233,
    248
   ],
   "subject": "boy"
  },
  {
   "text": "And the last people they fooled?",
   "words": [
    249,
    254
   ],
   "subject": "old_lou"
  },
  {
   "text": "Their own families.",
   "words": [
    255,
    257
   ],
   "subject": "old_lou"
  },
  {
   "text": "The secret lasted more than fifty years.",
   "words": [
    258,
    264
   ],
   "subject": "old_lou"
  }
 ],
